>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Single-point calculation on the original coordinates and ligand-by-ligand Lewis review. Both Cp rings have H5, Each carries −1; Two unsaturated carbons contact Zr directly, They serve as formal anionic termini. The phosphine has three C–P contacts. The P–C bond is assigned a lower order than a triple bond. This limiting form contains a dianionic diene fragment, two Cp⁻ ligands and Zr(IV), COD 4068698 supports H39. Localized 16 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

